In the context of food sovereignty, toxic leadership may involve leaders who prioritize profit over the well-being of the community, neglecting the needs of those who rely on the food system for their survival. This can result in poor food quality, lack of access to healthy food options, and increased vulnerability to food insecurity.

To address toxic leadership in the context of food sovereignty, it is important to promote transparency, accountability, and collaboration among stakeholders. This includes encouraging open communication, empowering local communities to make informed decisions about food production and distribution, and supporting policies that prioritize the well-being of all members of society.";
    string food sovereignty = "Food sovereignty is a concept that emphasizes the importance of local control over food production and distribution. It advocates for the rights of communities to decide how food is produced, distributed, and consumed, ensuring that food systems are sustainable, equitable, and responsive to the needs of the people.

In the context of toxic leadership, food sovereignty can be seen as a response to the negative impacts of toxic leadership on the food system. By promoting food sovereignty, communities can reclaim control over their food systems and work towards creating a more just and equitable food environment.";

    cout << "Key Concepts:" << endl;
    cout << "1. " << Toxic leadership << endl;
    cout << "2. " << Food sovereignty << endl;

